$\begin{align}
\left(7^3\right)^{3}&=7^{3\cdot 3}
\\\\
&=7^{9}
\end{align}$

This follows from the general rule $\left(x^m\right)^{n}=x^{m\cdot n}$.

We can also see this is correct by expanding the powers.

$\begin{align}
\left(7^3\right)^{3}&=\underbrace{7^3\cdot 7^3\cdot 7^3}_\text{3 times}
\\\\\\
&=\underbrace{
\underbrace{7\cdot 7\cdot 7}_\text{3 times}
\cdot \underbrace{7\cdot 7\cdot 7}_\text{3 times}
\cdot \underbrace{7\cdot 7\cdot 7}_\text{3 times}}
_\text{3 times}
\\\\
&=7^{9}
\end{align}$
